{"name":"Warm Up","hex":"#9e6654","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warm up","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become warmer.","To heat or reheat (e.g. food)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm_up"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warm Up (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Warm Up is the debut extended play (EP) by Spanish singer-songwriter Bad Gyal. It was released on 19 March 2021 by Aftercluv Dance Lab and Interscope Records, and it is her first full-length release after being signed with these two labels in 2019."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d9/Bad_Gyal_-_Warm_Up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warm_Up_(EP)"},{"title":"Warm Up!","blocks":[{"text":"Warm Up! is a 2000 single-player racing simulator developed by Lankhor and published by Microids for PlayStation and Windows."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Warm_Up%21_French_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warm_Up!"},{"title":"Warming up","blocks":[{"text":"Warming up is a part of stretching and preparation for physical exertion or a performance by exercising or practicing gently beforehand, usually undertaken before a performance or practice. Athletes, singers, actors and others warm up before stressing their muscles. It is widely believed to prepare the muscles for vigorous actions and to prevent muscle cramps and injury due to overexertion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Training_of_Seattle_Mist_Lingerie_Football_0154.jpg/330px-Training_of_Seattle_Mist_Lingerie_Football_0154.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warming_up"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Participants_with_the_Water_Warrior_c